From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fil Dunsky <filipp.dunsky@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 21:17:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: arm: cpus: Add Cortina Systems CS7542 enable
 method

On the CS7542 the bootloader parks the secondary Cortex-A9 core in a loop
that waits for an event and then jumps to the address found in a global
software register. Add the "cortina,cs7542-smp" enable method for it and,
as with the other release-address based methods, require cpu-release-addr
to point at that register.

Reviewed-by: Linus Walleij <linusw@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Fil Dunsky <filipp.dunsky@gmail.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261013-b4-cs75xx-v6-3-37e8f3969b7c@gmail.com
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/cpus.yaml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/cpus.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/cpus.yaml
@@ -247,6 +247,7 @@ properties:
           - brcm,bcm63138
           - brcm,bcm-nsp-smp
           - brcm,brahma-b15
+          - cortina,cs7542-smp
           - marvell,armada-375-smp
           - marvell,armada-380-smp
           - marvell,armada-390-smp
@@ -462,6 +463,7 @@ allOf:
         enable-method:
           enum:
             - spin-table
+            - cortina,cs7542-smp
             - renesas,r9a06g032-smp
       required:
         - enable-method
